					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1637405#post-2482687</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1637405/lessons-learned#post-2482687</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 31 Mar 2016 20:28:18 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dexanote</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>481882</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Part of it is that the Foundation doesn't exactly know what went down, why they broke so easily, who was part of it, etc. I used the vagueness of 5-6 years of referencing the Library Attack in irc as a basis for that theme.</p> <p>Which lantern? The one that wrecked the Agents, or the great writer?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1637405#post-2479978</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1637405/lessons-learned#post-2479978</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 27 Mar 2016 08:14:02 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Noxley</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1344310</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I like what this piece does to &quot;colour in&quot; the Wanderer's Library, and I like the touch of benevolence too. The lantern creature, for example, is perfect. Now that I think of it, it's kinda reminiscent of something out of a Hayao Miyazaki movie. My only problem is how quickly the foundation agents seem to just completely break and scatter, regardless of whatever tricks were played on them - they're slightly too much like scared children. No back up plans? No contingencies? What was the point of it, anyway - to just go in and shook the place up? Whatever the objective, it all seems to have been very poorly organised too. All in all, though, it works in the end.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
